WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:06.400
The wilcoxon test analyzes whether there's a&nbsp;
difference between two dependent samples or&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.400 --> 00:00:12.720
not. In dependent samples the measured&nbsp;
values are always available in pairs&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.720 --> 00:00:20.000
the pairs result from for example from repeated&nbsp;
measures of the same person. Therefore if you have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:26.320
two dependent groups and you want to test whether&nbsp;
there is a difference between these two groups&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.320 --> 00:00:32.880
then you can use the wilcoxon test. The&nbsp;
wilcoxon test is the non-parametric counterpart&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.880 --> 00:00:39.680
of the t-test for dependent samples. To put it&nbsp;
simple, if your data is not normally distributed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.680 --> 00:00:48.080
you use a non-parametric test, in the case of two&nbsp;
dependent samples this would be the wilcoxon test

